;; spec:   stdlib §2.3 (Lookup: no Set instance), §5.5 S2 (callable sets wait for L21)
;; expect: reject
;; error:  no implementation of Lookup for (Set i64)
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; covers: get
;; Clojure's (get #{1 2} 1) answers the element, 1. The page's Lookup has
;; instances for Map, Vec, Array and str but not Set (the table of §2.3): a
;; Set is asked with contains?, and the element lookup comes with callable
;; sets (L21). So a get on a Set is the compile error above, never a wrong
;; answer; the day an instance lands this case is deleted in the commit
;; that lands it.
(ns main (:use fib.core fib.seq fib.coll))

(defun main () -> i64
  (match (get (set [1 2]) 1) ((some x) x) (nil 0)))
